</div></div><a href="#" class="closebtn">×</a></div></div></nav><div class="site-inner"><div class="content-sidebar-wrap"><main class="content" id="genesis-content"><nav id="breadcrumbs" aria-label="breadcrumbs"><span><span><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/">Home</a></span> &gt; <span><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/category/recipe/">Recipes</a></span></span></nav><article class="post-562 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail category-food category-recipe category-salsas mv-content-wrapper entry" aria-label="Easy Restaurant Style Salsa"><header class="entry-header"><h1 class="entry-title">Easy Restaurant Style Salsa</h1>
<p class="entry-meta">Published: <time class="entry-time">Jul 13, 2015</time> · Modified: <time class="entry-modified-time">Mar 19, 2024</time> by <span class="entry-author"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/" class="entry-author-link" rel="author"><span class="entry-author-name">Ana</span></a></span> · This post may contain affiliate links · <span class="entry-comments-link"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/easy-restaurant-style-salsa/#comments">37 Comments</a></span></p></header><div class="entry-content"><div class="wprm-recipe wprm-recipe-snippet wprm-recipe-template-emk-snippet-buttons"><a href="#recipe" data-recipe="2784" style="color: #ffffff;background-color: #000000;border-color: #ffffff;border-radius: 3px;padding: 3px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-jump wprm-recipe-link wprm-jump-to-recipe-shortcode wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-jump-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent">Jump to Recipe</a>
<a href="https://www.pinterest.com/pin/create/bookmarklet/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.espressomykitchen.com%2Feasy-restaurant-style-salsa%2F&amp;media=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.espressomykitchen.com%2Fwp-content%2Fuploads%2F2024%2F01%2FEMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3.jpg&amp;description=Easy+Restaurant+Style+Salsa&amp;is_video=false" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" data-recipe="2784" data-url="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/easy-restaurant-style-salsa/" data-media="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3.jpg" data-description="Easy Restaurant Style Salsa" data-repin="" role="button" style="color: #ffffff;background-color: #000000;border-color: #ffffff;border-radius: 3px;padding: 3px 8px;" class="wprm-recipe-pin wprm-recipe-link wprm-block-text-normal wprm-recipe-pin-inline-button wprm-recipe-link-inline-button wprm-color-accent">Pin Recipe</a></div>
<p>My favorite part when going to Mexican restaurants is the complimentary chips and salsa. Seriously though, that combo of crunchy tortilla chips and salsa is so simple, yet so delicious. So, why not make this easy restaurant&nbsp;style&nbsp;salsa recipe at home to have when you are craving some chips and salsa.&nbsp;Homemade salsa is a must in our fridge at all times. It taste fresh and does not have the extra additives from the store bought ones.&nbsp;&nbsp;It’s super easy and flavorful and always so satisfying.&nbsp;</p>


<div class="wp-block-image">
<figure class="aligncenter size-full"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3.jpg"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" fetchpriority="high" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3.jpg" alt="restaurant style salsa served in a small bowl with tortilla chip dipped into the salsa and tortilla chips on the side" data-skip-lazy class="wp-image-10090" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3.jpg 1200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-3-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></a></figure>
</div>


<p>This recipe makes about a cup, which last about 3-4 days in our fridge.  Its no surprise we really love our salsas here. If we're craving a green salsa this <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/roasted-tomatillo-salsa/">roasted tomatillo salsa </a>is our go-to or when we want something more of an everyday salsa then this <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/spicy-mexican-red-salsa/">red spicy salsa </a>is a must! For a smoky salsa then you must try <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/chile-morita-salsa/">morita salsa.</a> For that extra heat then this <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/roasted-habanero-salsa/">roasted habanero salsa</a> is a must!</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Why you'll love this recipe</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Only fresh ingredients are needed </li>



<li>It's super easy to make</li>



<li>The spice level can be adjusted to your taste</li>



<li>Super addicting with tortilla chips</li>



<li>A crowd pleaser</li>
</ul>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Ingredients you will need</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Tomato </strong>- 2 large ripe tomatoes</li>



<li><strong>Cilantro -</strong> 3-4 sprigs to add that extra freshness</li>



<li><strong>Jalapeño</strong> - seeds and membranes removed</li>



<li><strong>Chile de árbo</strong>l - seeds removed</li>



<li><strong>Oregano </strong>- a little dash of oregano</li>



<li><strong>Kosher salt</strong> - for taste</li>



<li><strong>Onion -</strong> white or yellow onion work here</li>
</ul>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1.jpg"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1.jpg" alt="restaurant style salsa ingredient on countertop" class="wp-image-10092" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1.jpg 1200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-ingredients-1-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></a></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to make restaurant style salsa</h2>



<p>Start by roasting tomato, garlic clove, jalapeños and  árbol chiles for about 5 minutes. Add all ingredients to a food processor or blender and add 3-4 cilantro sprigs, ¼ cup white onion and salt and blend until smooth. If salsa is too thick add ¼ cup of water or more until you have reach desire consistency. Add more salt if needed and serve with your favorite tortilla chips. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-3 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex">
<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1.jpg"><img decoding="async" width="683" height="1024" data-id="10093" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1-683x1024.jpg" alt="tomatoes, jalapeños, garlic clove and arbol chilis roasting on a pan with olive oil" class="wp-image-10093" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-1.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 683px) 100vw, 683px" /></a></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="683" height="1024" data-id="10094" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2-683x1024.jpg" alt="overhead shot of all ingredients inside a food processor" class="wp-image-10094" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-2.jpg 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 683px) 100vw, 683px" /></a></figure>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-large"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="683" height="1024" data-id="10095" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3-683x1024.jpg" alt="overhead shot of blended salsa inside a food processor" class="wp-image-10095" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3-150x225.jpg 150w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-step-3.jpg 1200w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 683px) 100vw, 683px" /></a></figure>
</figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Substitutions</h2>



<p><strong>Tomato </strong>- You can certainly replace the tomatos with can of 14 oz  whole tomatoes.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Storage suggestions</h2>



<p>You can store in the fridge in airtight container for up to seven days. You can also freeze for up to 4 months but it will lose it's freshness over time. </p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to serve this salsa</h2>



<p>You can serve with tortilla chips, but can also be used in <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/web-stories/instant-pot-shredded-beef-tacos/">tacos</a>, <a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/the-ultimate-california-burrito/">burritos</a>, and any of your favorite Mexican dishes. </p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><a href="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2.jpg"><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1800" src="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2.jpg" alt="hand holding a tortilla chip scooping salsa into chip" class="wp-image-10089" srcset="https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2.jpg 1200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2-200x300.jpg 200w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2-683x1024.jpg 683w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://www.espressomykitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/EMK-restaurant-style-salsa-hero-2-150x225.jpg 150w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /></a></figure>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Variations</h2>



<p><strong>Mild</strong> - Use one jalapeño and one chile de árbol and remove all the seeds and membranes<br><strong>Hot-</strong>  use 1 ½  jalapeños and 2 chile de árbol and remove all the seeds <br><strong>Spicy </strong>- Use 2 jalapeños and 3 chile de árbol and keep some of the seeds </p>


